From e883cd6ce8fb71bf714379cee1d87661e36e04e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sitaram Bulusu <sitaram.bulusu@seamless.se>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:24:05 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] airoha: en751221: add TP-Link XZ000-G3 v1

Same board as the v2 (EN7521S, 64 MiB DDR2, EN7571, one GbE port,
reset on GPIO 0, PON LED on GPIO 2, LOS LED on GPIO 7) but with a
16 MiB XMC XM25QH128A SPI-NOR instead of the 4 MiB EN25QH32.

The stock v1 layout already keeps factoryinfo at 0x40000, loid at
0x50000 and hwinfo at 0x60000, so they stay in place and nothing
per-unit is rewritten. migrate_layout only replaces the boot area
(tcboot, romfile, bootflag) after the image and the stock factoryinfo
pass their checks. The stock A/B images, config, iot and "other"
areas become one 15.5 MiB firmware partition at 0x70000.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
